{"attack":true,"case":"The target's stated dependence is circular and self-refuting: the piecewise-linear cost-function analogy (supposedly supplied by SRC_005) is actually supplied by the target itself (SRC_004), so the 'causal mechanism' justifying the 9/180/603 partition is not inherited from SRC_005 at all.\nThe target says 'the piecewise-linear cost-function analogy ... supplies the explanatory causal mechanism that justifies why the digit-budget partition into 9, 180, and 603 is the correct decomposition,' and that it is refuted if SRC_004's partition can be motivated by the base-10 positional system alone. But the analogy is introduced in the target (SRC_004) itself, not in SRC_005, and the support content shows the partition 9 + 180 + 603 = 792 is already established by the base-10 positional numeral system (9 one-digit pages, 90 two-digit pages contributing 180, and 201 three-digit pages contributing 603). The target therefore states its own refutation condition as satisfied: the partition is fully motivated by base-10 positional structure without any recourse to the step-function/resource-consumption framework. Asserting dependence on SRC_005 for an analogy that the target itself supplies and that is not needed is a substantive fault: the named dependence relation is empty, making the target a summary of endpoints rather than a genuine relation.\ncites: 930b5d801b392134a75969ad9039ca6d936402d12fdff03e2f58a5f749b85e99"}